%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4b3f2a8c8f344355b16a4d4296ae3f98, type: 3}
  m_Name: Urchin
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  vesselClass: 4
  entries:
  - Element: 1
    AbilityLabel: Chain Spikes
    AbilityDescription: One trigger, two shots. TAP it for an aimed shotgun of spikes
      out of both guns; HOLD it to charge and RELEASE for a burst in every direction,
      with the spike count taken from how long you held. Every spike embeds in the
      prism it hits, steals it, and sprays the next generation out of the mass it just
      took - a cascade that runs for as long as it keeps finding enemy territory. Charge
      is the weapon's whole ENERGY - how far each spike flies and how deep the chain
      runs. At level 5 the cascade gains a generation and stops losing reach as it spreads.
    Input: 1
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 2.5
    MinMultiplier: 0.4
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Overcharge
    UpgradeDescription: The cascade runs one generation deeper AND stops decaying.
      Normally each generation launches shorter than the one before it, so a deep
      cascade peters out; overcharged, it goes further and the last generation reaches
      as far as the first.
  - Element: 2
    AbilityLabel: Trail Rider
    AbilityDescription: Fly into a trail to latch onto it and ride, steering by the
      ribbon rather than the stick. Your own trail GROWS under you as you pass;
      an enemy's is STOLEN. Riding also recharges ammo, at double rate over shielded
      prisms. Ride off the END of a ribbon and you launch, keeping the speed the grind
      was doing. Mass is how much volume each friendly prism gains per pass. Passive -
      it triggers on contact, not on a button.
    Input: 0
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Reinforced Wake
    UpgradeDescription: Prisms you grow while riding arrive shielded. Since a shielded
      prism pays double ammo to ride over, a fortified lap of your own trail funds
      the next one.
  - Element: 3
    AbilityLabel: Track Projector
    AbilityDescription: Project a straight stretch of single-track trail out in front
      of you - a rail to launch off where the map has none. It is ordinary mass in your
      own domain, so you ride it at friendly speed, grow it as you pass, and anyone else
      can take it from you. Space is how LONG the stretch is. Twenty-second cooldown.
      At level 5 the projection runs a further hundred units.
    Input: 2
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Long Haul
    UpgradeDescription: The projected track is laid a hundred units longer. A longer
      rail is a longer grind - more ammo recharged, more prisms grown, and more speed
      carried off the far end.
  - Element: 4
    AbilityLabel: Slip
    AbilityDescription: Let go of the trail you are riding and phase out for a moment,
      so you can clear the mass you were inside instead of being re-latched by it.
      Time is how long the ghost lasts. At level 5 hostile trail no longer slows you
      down, so raiding an enemy ribbon is as fast as riding your own.
    Input: 7
    MultiplierAtFullLevel: 1
    MinMultiplier: 1
    UnlockLevel: 5
    RelockBelowLevel: 4
    LatchPolicy: 0
    UpgradeLabel: Slipstream
    UpgradeDescription: Enemy trail is ridden at your friendly speed. Hostile mass
      normally crawls, which punishes the raid exactly when you most want to be
      moving; overcharged, you cross it at full pace while still converting it.
